        "answer": {
          "short": "$x+2y-18=0$.\n\nThe perpendicular gradient is $-\\frac12$ and the line passes through $(4,7)$.",
          "worked": "The perpendicular gradient is $-\\frac12$, since $2\\times\\left(-\\frac12\\right)=-1$. Using $C(4,7)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-7&=-\\frac12(x-4)\\\\2(y-7)&=-(x-4)\\\\2y-14&=-x+4\\\\x+2y-18&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
